    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.23.0</title>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:08:21 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22300</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.23.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>New words that fit the pond: a pond's working folders are <strong>streams</strong> (their git branch shown beside them) and an agent's helpers are <strong>ducklings</strong>.</li><li>Every thread is a duck in its own colour, the same on your Mac and iPhone, with a small Claude or Codex badge.</li><li>New streams get names like Mossy Creek or Recursive Mallard; New stream suggests one and can roll another.</li><li>Signing in is a page in Squeak's window. Squeak comes back to the front when you finish in the browser.</li><li>Every thread's agent knows it runs in Squeak, and knows who is talking when several people write in one thread.</li></ul><ul><li>Shared threads show the machine they run on, while local threads keep their own branch and routing.</li><li>Pond settings has clearer sections and shortcuts, wrapping colour choices, an Add label button and collapsible action prompts.</li><li>Dropdowns stay close to the control you clicked, highlight it while open, and stay attached when the window resizes.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.22.3</h4><ul><li>Pond dashboards have searchable branches and threads, live summary filters, and a responsive Flock and Ripples column.</li><li>Drag ponds in the sidebar to put them in your own order; the filter menu switches between My order and Recent activity.</li><li>Pond rows show they can be clicked when you hover.</li><li>Check for updates in the sidebar no longer flickers: the icon spins and one line says Checking…, then Up to date.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.22.2</h4><ul><li>In-app dropdowns, pickers and context menus use Squeak's own menu surfaces, with keyboard navigation, selection marks and shortcut hints.</li><li>New pond and New branch text fields are taller, with more space around the text and a clear focus border.</li><li>The next-thread button says Next update or Next request and aligns with the composer, in its own row so it never covers message text.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
